    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1144">

                <pb facs="0946" n="936" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg936"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.6336/2–1249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-12T08:00:00+08:00">February 12,
                            1949—8 a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 12—2:32 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>218. ReContel 208, February 10.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d1144-f1"/> On basis
                    personal experience Mukden conditions, adduce following possible alternative
                    explanations difficulties Consulate there apparently experiencing: (1)
                    Communists, as previously suggested, may have suspected Consulate transmitting
                    messages for Chinese Government agencies (whether Consulate did so through
                    normal channels would presumably be known Embassy Nanking) or (2) previous …
                    connections may have involved Consulate.…</p>
                <p>ReDeptel 54, January 31.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d1144-f2"/> Believe it inadvisable
                    until position Consulate clarified send Manhard<anchor n="10" xml:id="d1144-f3"
                    /> or other officer now: (1) Seems clear personnel Mukden unable perform
                    fruitful work at present and (2) new officer arriving might fall in same
                    position as officers already there. Understand persons traveling Manchuria must
                    have Manchurian residence certificates, request authority if feasible send
                    Chinese messenger, preferably former Mukden employee if willing, to check on
                    position Consulate and return to report. This procedure would be adopted after
                    making local representations regarding Mukden–Tientsin communications and
                    coordination Tientsin.</p>
                <p>Repeated Nanking 175.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
